From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:34:23 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve localized resources through the bundle's table cache
 (#1686)

On macOS 26, String(localized:) on a LocalizedStringResource reads and
parses the whole string table on every call. The palette resolves
command names, kind labels and section titles that way on each render,
so translated builds stutter and English pays a smaller cost.

resolved() looks the key up through Bundle.main's cached table and
falls back to String(localized:) whenever the result needs the
resource's arguments or its default value, so every string is unchanged.
